summary:
  An answer whose last hop Qt does not name is reported like no answer at
  all, so the second look counts it towards a silent address.

history:
  The probe gave 0 both when nobody answered and when somebody did but Qt
  left the place unnamed. Silence on three looks moves a station; on a Qt
  that never names the last hop a living address would give nothing but such
  answers and be moved after fifteen minutes. The two are told apart now: 0
  for silence, -1 for an answer with no place, and -1 never moves anything.

target:
  package/contents/ui/KinHunt.qml

find:
                      finish(status === 0 ? 0 : -1, "", "");

replace:
                      finish(0, "", "");

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_kinhunt.qml::test_an_answer_with_no_place_is_told_apart_from_no_answer
  and tests/qml/tst_kinhunt.qml::test_an_answer_with_no_place_never_becomes_a_move.
  Line-neutral.
